PART 6️⃣ — Exactly-Once Myth in Kafka (VERY IMPORTANT)

Kafka Exactly-Once ≠ Business Exactly-Once

> Kafka can guarantee exactly-once delivery to Kafka topics, NOT to your database or services.

What Kafka Exactly-Once REALLY Means

✔ Producer → Kafka  
✔ Kafka → Kafka Streams  

❌ Kafka → DB  
❌ Kafka → External API  

Example (Illusion)

java
db.save(order);   // success
crash();          // before commit offset

➡ Kafka retries  
➡ DB save happens AGAIN

❌ Not exactly-once

How Kafka Achieves EOS (Internally)

- Idempotent producer
- Transactional producer
- Offset + produce in same transaction

Why it breaks in microservices

| Step | System |
|----|----|
| Consume | Kafka |
| Save | DB |
| Publish | Kafka |

❌ Cannot span DB + Kafka transaction

Real-world Solution (Truth)

> Design idempotent consumers + outbox pattern + at-least-once delivery

Correct Mental Model

| Myth | Reality |
|----|----|
| Exactly once | At least once |
| Kafka handles consistency | Application handles it |
| No duplicates | Expect duplicates |

