6️⃣ What Controller is NOT

Let’s clear wrong mental models:

❌ Controller is NOT a REST controller  
❌ Controller does NOT handle messages  
❌ Controller does NOT process producers/consumers  
❌ Controller is NOT always the same broker  

7️⃣ Example: Broker Failure Scenario (REAL FLOW)

Initial state

Partition P0 leader → Broker-1
Controller → Broker-3

Broker-1 crashes

What happens step by step
1️⃣ Controller notices broker heartbeat missing  
2️⃣ Controller selects new leader (Broker-2)  
3️⃣ Controller updates metadata  
4️⃣ Controller notifies all brokers  
5️⃣ Producers & consumers refresh metadata  

✔ Zero ZooKeeper/KRaft involvement in decision logic  
✔ They only coordinate election

8️⃣ Why only ONE controller?

Because:
- Multiple controllers → conflicting leader elections
- Split-brain scenario
- Inconsistent metadata

👉 Exactly one source of truth

